AI Travel Itinerary Generator — Refined Product Requirements Document (PRD)

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
The Big Picture:
The AI Travel Itinerary Generator is a web-based application that produces personalized, day-by-day travel plans using a combination of AI creativity (OpenAI API) and real-world data (Google Places API).
The Problem We Solve:
Users spend excessive time planning trips using multiple sources and tools. This app centralizes itinerary planning into a single, intelligent platform capable of generating coherent, realistic travel plans in seconds.
Our Target User:
Frequent travelers, students, and busy professionals seeking quick travel planning assistance in their native language.
Core Capabilities (MVP):
AI-powered itinerary creation with minimal inputs
Itinerary viewing and editing
Authentication (optional guest mode)
Map view per day (pins and coordinates)
Multilingual interface selection
Complexity Snapshot:
Architectural Complexity: Moderate – Standard CRUD app orchestrating external APIs
External Service Integrations: Limited to OpenAI API and Google Places API
Business Logic Depth: Medium – merging AI generation with geodata
MVP Success Criteria:
A user can generate, view, and save an itinerary in <4 seconds.
Travel plans integrate verified Google data and function in one language.
Basic map integration and itinerary management available end-to-end.

1. USERS & PERSONAS
Primary Persona: The Smart Traveler (Alex)
Motivation: Create a quick, practical itinerary without researching every location manually.
Pain Point: Overload of travel information online, lacking structure.
Goal: Reliable trip plan within minutes.

2. FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
2.1 Core MVP Features
FR-001: AI Itinerary Generation
Description: Uses OpenAI and Google Places APIs to generate realistic itineraries.
Entity Type: Itinerary (User-Generated Content)
Lifecycle Operations:
Create: Input destination and duration, generate itinerary.
Read: Display structured plan per day.
Update: Regenerate or edit daily content.
Delete: Remove saved itineraries.
List/Search: List all user itineraries with date/destination filters.
Acceptance Criteria:
[ ] Itinerary generated within 4 seconds.
[ ] Includes real attractions and restaurants.
FR-002: Basic Map Integration
Description: Display itinerary on Google Maps with daily pins.
Lifecycle Operations:
Create/View: Map auto-renders existing locations.
Update: Re-render pins after itinerary edits.
Acceptance Criteria:
[ ] Pins show relevant data (name, rating).
FR-003: User Authentication (Minimal)
Description: Standard login/signup + guest mode access.
Lifecycle Operations:
Create: Register via email/password.
Update: Edit profile name/language.
Delete: Delete account.
Acceptance Criteria:
[ ] JWT or Firebase Auth.
[ ] Guest users receive sharable itineraries.
FR-004: Itinerary Management
Description: Users can create, view, edit, or delete itineraries.
Acceptance Criteria:
[ ] CRUD operations stored in DB.
[ ] PDF export deferred.

