6. MVP COMPLEXITY & SCALABILITY
Complexity Level: Moderate
Critical Dependencies: OpenAI + Google Places APIs
Optimization: Cache API responses and batch map calls
Expected Load: 10K itineraries/month

7. DEFERRED INTEGRATIONS
No booking APIs or export services in MVP. All integrations (translation, share links) deferred to later sprints.

8. MVP SCOPE & SUCCESS DEFINITION
In Scope:
End-to-end itinerary creation, view, and save functionality.
Basic map view (Google Maps).
Simple user authentication.
Deferred:
PDF export, multi-language support, public link sharing, advanced maps.
MVP Success =
User successfully generates and views a usable itinerary within 4 seconds, proving AI-assisted travel planning works.

9. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
Performance: ≤4 second API response
Security: JWT-based auth
Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 AA
Availability: 99.5% uptime

10. ASSUMPTIONS & DECISIONS
No payment or booking API integration.
English-only interface to start.
Target modern browsers (Chromium, Safari).
Focus: Single-user experience validation.

PRD Complete – Ready for architect and UI/UX agents.


